OpenDIA -- Complete OpenDIA analysis of DIA runs: raw spectra to precursor q-values.
Full documentation: http://www.openms.de/doxygen/nightly/html/TOPP_OpenDIA.html
Version: 3.7.0-pre-exported-20261124 Nov 24 2026, 16:40:06
To cite OpenMS:
 + Pfeuffer, J., Bielow, C., Wein, S. et al.. OpenMS 3 enables reproducible analysis of large-scale mass spectrometry data. Nat Methods (2024). doi:10.1038/s41592-024-02197-7.

Usage:
  OpenDIA <options>

Options (mandatory options marked with '*'):
  -in <files>*         DIA runs (Thermo raw, mzML, ...)
  -lib <file>*         Library (PQP or OpenDIA .parquet) with decoys named DECOY_<target TRAML_ID> (search fragments, up to 6 per precursor). A PQP is converted once to <stem>.opendia.parquet next to it, which later runs read instead (valid formats: 'pqp', 'parquet', 'pqt')
